# Build output. dist/ alone is ~129MB and is regenerated by
# tools/build_exe.py, so it has no business in version control — and the zip
# inside it is far past what GitHub accepts for a repository file anyway.
# Release assets are where that belongs.
dist/
build/
*.spec

# Player state, not project state. Written next to the source when running
# from a working copy, and in %LOCALAPPDATA% once packaged.
savegame.json
_selftest_save.json

# Diagnostic renders from tools/audio_mix_check.py and the like.
audio_mix_sample.wav
*_preview.png
cmp_*.png

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# Generated art and audio ARE committed. They are ~23MB, which is well within
# what a repository should carry, and committing them means a fresh clone can
# build straight away instead of needing the generators run first. Delete
# these lines and add assets/ if that ever stops being the right trade.

# Claude Code's per-machine permission state. Absolute paths to this
# machine's temp directories, and the filename says local. A shared
# .claude/settings.json would be committed; this one should not be.
.claude/settings.local.json
